WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.550
Every manager has a strong side.

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.350
And sides they keep meaning to improve,

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.350
but never quite get to.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:16.390
So every manager needs support on three sides: the operational side, the human side, and daily situations that call for a second opinion.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:21.770
And each person's aspirations can get lost between meetings, Slack and notes.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.710
It's like a spotlight on whoever speaks the most.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.240
The quiet ones wait their turn.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:32.820
Now, AI can support all three, alongside HR and your own manager,

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:34.880
while the thinking stays yours.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.440
And it helps most where you're less strong.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:44.420
One manager uses an AI companion so everyone gets regular, consistent feedback that follows good practice.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:50.320
So in this adventure, you build a management companion with skills and one automation,

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:52.800
then check both of you for bias.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.500
And its first test:

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:57.460
what should I cover in each 1:1 this week?
